                        "glosses": [
                            "Resembling vapor; vaporous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29a63848-a639-47d5-b19f-61af3c562230",
                                "sense_id": "e3405837-a39e-3410-82e6-009a56948907",
                                "text": "But here again, Christians consider the word literally, as though the Lord would appear upon the vapory clouds over our heads."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa9f177c-8b8f-4662-9e7d-636e4ea869bd",
                                "sense_id": "e3405837-a39e-3410-82e6-009a56948907",
                                "text": "The greatest damps however, that may ever roll upon your spirits, will arise from the stupidity of sinners, and the vapory dullness of declining Christians."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb05a574-ee7d-4275-81cb-35a55436f156",
                                "sense_id": "e3405837-a39e-3410-82e6-009a56948907",
                                "text": "Long at the window he stood, and wistfully gazed on the landscape, / Washed with a cold gray mist, the vapory breath of the east-wind,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4eba4556-581b-4207-84cf-bbf06d3040db",
                                "sense_id": "e3405837-a39e-3410-82e6-009a56948907",
                                "text": "At the same moment it chanced that the vapory fleece hanging low in the East, was shot thro' with a soft glory as of the fleece of the Lamb of God seen in mystical vision, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2237ebf5-ba61-4462-83e8-7715af957edd",
                                "sense_id": "e3405837-a39e-3410-82e6-009a56948907",
                                "text": "See also quotations under vapoury."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35d6f208-0aae-34eb-be4e-49371b8defb7",
                        "entry_id": "b0493ec8-18a4-363a-bfed-369b4720c069",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characterized by the presence of vapor; full of, or obscured by, vapor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5748f855-ebcd-494c-8338-a8f367b8f1ec",
                                "sense_id": "35d6f208-0aae-34eb-be4e-49371b8defb7",
                                "text": "The most fetid and poisonous smells everywhere prevailed; and by the aid of that ghastly light which, even at midnight, never fails to emanate from a vapory and pestilential atmosphere, might be discerned lying in the by-paths and alleys, or rotting in the windowless habitations, the carcass of many a nocturnal plunderer arrested by the hand of the plague in the very perpetration of his robbery."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
